@startuml 05-sequence-secrets
title FlowAI Platform - Secret Lifecycle (sequence)

autonumber

participant "Operator" as Op
participant "Web UI" as UI
participant "Secret Service" as SS
participant "Automation" as Auto
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Event Router" as ER
participant "Executor Queue" as qexec
participant "Executor" as EX
participant "Agent Container" as AG

note over Op, SS
  Operator manages secrets via Web UI. Secret Service is the only CRUD client.
end note

== Operator creates secret ==

Op -> UI : Open Secrets page
UI -> SS : POST /secrets { name, value, scope }
SS -> SS : Encrypt, persist (audit logged)
SS --> UI : 201 secret_id
UI --> Op : Secret saved

note over Auto, EX
  Task time. API Gateway knows only secret_ids, builds scope.
  Event Router handles queue take-and-put for dispatch.
end note

== Submit ==

Auto -> GW : POST /tasks { prompt, tools, secret_ids: [a, b] }
GW -> GW : Build scope = HMAC(project_id, task_id, secret_ids, TTL)
GW -> GW : Persist task
GW --> Auto : 202 task_id

== Dispatch (event-router take-and-put) ==

ER -> GW : resolve task_id -> task_spec + scope_token
GW --> ER : task_spec + scope_token
ER -> qexec : put on per-executor queue
ER --> EX : poll q:exec-X -> deliver task_spec + scope_token
EX -> EX : Pull image

== Secret resolve ==

EX -> SS : POST /secrets/get-by-scope { scope_token }
SS -> SS : Validate scope signature, expiry, project
SS --> EX : { "a": "...", "b": "..." }
EX -> AG : Start container, mount secrets as env / tmpfs

note over AG
  Has secrets from start. No runtime fetch needed unless refreshed.
end note

note over AG, EX
  On task end. Container terminated. Scope token expires. Plaintext gone.
end note

@enduml